# Embedded wash VM sudo policy.
#
# wash-router runs as the unprivileged `wash` user (see
# /etc/init.d/S99wash-router). wash-priv calls sudo to elevate
# specific app spawns to root. NOPASSWD because:
#
#   - The VM is a single-tenant, ephemeral browser sandbox; there
#     is no untrusted neighbour user to defend against.
#   - There's no realistic way to prompt for a sudo password in
#     this deployment — the user hasn't set one (BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_
#     ROOT_PASSWD="" + empty wash password via the users table).
#   - wash-priv's startup probe (`sudo -n true`) detects this and
#     skips the FE password modal accordingly.
#
# For a real (non-embedded) deployment, replace this file with one
# that omits NOPASSWD; wash-priv will then prompt for the password
# via its FE modal + P-256 ECDH handshake the way it normally would.
wash ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
